# Stage 1B β — Pre-S Decision After Active L Writes

## Alignment

- **Module touched:** Stage 1B β measurement/control only
- **Product vs implementation:** execution control for L-vs-S pilot
- **Architecture-doc consistency:** preserves signed-off β design: L and S run sequentially, same corpus, same current codebase, only env-var differs
- **Drift risk:** treating a moving mid-L snapshot as final; starting S before L finishes; overstating what β proves when L does not mutate global ontology
- **Out of scope:** Stage 2, prompt changes, MultiModelExtractor changes, `brain/app.py`, Gardener changes, Data Gates, v2, Nexus 100 scoring, workflow restarts, `replit.md` edits

## Decision

Do **not** start S.

L is still actively writing extraction outputs. The earlier `100/100 docs both models` marker was only Phase-1 per-model extraction completion, not full pipeline completion.

Strict sequential control remains in force.

## Decision 1 — Frozen snapshot

Use option **(b)**.

Do not treat the 21:51 snapshot as frozen. Treat it as a mid-L snapshot.

Final L snapshot is captured only after all of these are true:

```text
L workflow exited successfully
no active L extraction process remains
entity total stable across two polls at least 2 minutes apart
relationship total stable across two polls at least 2 minutes apart
global ontology.types unchanged from pre-L
global ontology.relations unchanged from pre-L
S graph outputs still empty before S
````

The 21:51 snapshot should be kept as evidence of L still writing, but not used as the L baseline.

## Decision 2 — Ontology-write path interpretation

The `staging_loader.py` ontology-write path is not a stop trigger by itself.

Record it as:

```text
Path exists.
It is called defensively to ensure entity_type exists.
It only inserts into ontology.types when LOWER(type_name) is missing from active ontology.types.
For Nexus L, it did not fire: ontology.types / ontology.relations counts and timestamps stayed unchanged.
```

Do not edit `staging_loader.py`.

Continue checking global ontology state until L exits.

## Decision 3 — β still proceeds after L stabilizes

Do not stop β.

But revise the β interpretation:

```text
For this corpus, β does not test ontology-growth suppression because L did not mutate global ontology. β tests scoped prompt execution and extraction-output differences.
```

The S run is still valuable because it tests:

```text
scoped prompts execute under CF_PIECE2_SCOPED_EXTRACTION=true
core + primary_domain are included
NULL-domain rows are excluded
other named domains are excluded
organizational relations survive after Piece 0.6
entity / relationship counts and type distributions differ or remain stable
audit_records behave as expected
```

Update the findings doc with this limitation.

## Authorized read-only check before S

Run a read-only grep/read of:

```text
CF_PIECE2_SCOPED_EXTRACTION
enforce_scoped_prompts
```

Goal:

```text
confirm the flag controls scoped prompt behavior, not ontology-write behavior.
```

Do not change code.

Report the call path.

## Decision 4 — Polling

Continue waiting for L.

Poll roughly every 10 minutes.

At each poll, report:

```text
timestamp
L workflow status
entities total
relationships total
entity delta from previous poll
relationship delta from previous poll
audit_records count
global ontology.types count
global ontology.relations count
ontology rows created/updated since L start
```

Do not kill or restart L.

Do not start S until L exits and counts stabilize.

## Final post-L checks before S

When L exits and counts stabilize:

```text
capture final L snapshot
compare final L snapshot to mid-L snapshots
confirm global ontology unchanged
confirm S graph still empty
confirm EXTRACTION_SYSTEM_PROMPT SHA unchanged
capture pre-S global ontology snapshot
```

If clean, start S.

## Stop triggers

Stop and report before S if:

```text
L workflow fails
L workflow does not exit after a materially concerning runtime
entity/relationship totals keep changing after workflow exit
global ontology.types changes
global ontology.relations changes
staging_loader ontology-write path appears to have fired
S graph is no longer empty before S
S would start before L is stable
```

